import{_ as n,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 248 | Realm Comparison · Dragon Ball: The Unanchored State of Power Inflation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 248 | Realm Comparison · Dragon Ball: The Unanchored State of Power Inflation","no":248,"module":1,"tags":["Realm Comparison","Dragon Ball","Power Inflation","Unanchored"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","244-Realm and Future Infinite Expandability","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0248_模块1-境界对比-龙珠体系战力膨胀的无锚状态.md","filePath":"en/0248_模块1-境界对比-龙珠体系战力膨胀的无锚状态.md"}'),r={name:"en/0248_模块1-境界对比-龙珠体系战力膨胀的无锚状态.md"};function i(s,e,l,u,d,g){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-248-realm-comparison-·-dragon-ball-the-unanchored-state-of-power-inflation" tabindex="-1">Entry 248 | Realm Comparison · Dragon Ball: The Unanchored State of Power Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-248-realm-comparison-·-dragon-ball-the-unanchored-state-of-power-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 248 | Realm Comparison · Dragon Ball: The Unanchored State of Power Inflation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 04, 244, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-infinite-inflation-from-power-level-5-to-super-saiyan-god" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Infinite inflation from power level 5 to Super Saiyan God <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-infinite-inflation-from-power-level-5-to-super-saiyan-god" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Infinite inflation from power level 5 to Super Saiyan God&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s realm system is rooted in law self-consistency, while Dragon Ball&#39;s power system is characterized by &quot;unanchored inflation&quot; — from the early &quot;power level 5&quot; to the late &quot;Super Saiyan God,&quot; power numbers and forms continuously upgrade, early settings repeatedly overturned. Dragon Ball&#39;s realm inflation is not based on law logic, but on the vicious cycle of &quot;enemies get stronger → protagonist must get stronger.&quot;</p><p>The six top-level axioms run through the comparison throughout: the anti-predation axiom points out Dragon Ball&#39;s combat essence; the republican axiom of Myriad Races contrasts Dragon Ball&#39;s personal heroism; the collective ascension axiom contrasts Dragon Ball&#39;s single-person invincibility; the causal self-discipline axiom contrasts Dragon Ball&#39;s casual resurrection; the law-first axiom directly points to Dragon Ball&#39;s setting self-consistency problem; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-dragon-ball-s-power-inflation-trajectory" tabindex="-1">I. Dragon Ball&#39;s Power Inflation Trajectory <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-dragon-ball-s-power-inflation-trajectory" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Dragon Ball&#39;s Power Inflation Trajectory&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s power system has undergone multiple stages of inflation:</p><ul><li><strong>Early arc</strong>: measured by &quot;power level&quot; numbers, Raditz&#39;s power level around 1000</li><li><strong>Namek arc</strong>: Super Saiyan, power level over 100 million</li><li><strong>Cell Games arc</strong>: beyond Super Saiyan</li><li><strong>Buu arc</strong>: fusion, Gotenks and other new forms</li><li><strong>Battle of Gods arc</strong>: Super Saiyan God</li><li><strong>Dragon Ball Super arc</strong>: Super Blue, Ultra Instinct, Perfected Ultra Instinct...</li></ul><p>Every stage needs new forms to face new enemies; power inflation has no end.</p><h2 id="ii-the-core-problem-of-unanchored-state" tabindex="-1">II. The Core Problem of &quot;Unanchored State&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-core-problem-of-unanchored-state" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Core Problem of &quot;Unanchored State&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s fundamental problem is <strong>no law anchor</strong> — power advancement is not based on understanding laws, but on &quot;transformations&quot; and &quot;training out new modes.&quot; This causes:</p><ul><li><strong>Vague realm definitions</strong>: Super Saiyan 1, 2, 3, God, Blue, Ultra Instinct... are these realms or forms?</li><li><strong>Numbers meaningless</strong>: power level numbers completely fail late, because numbers are too large to compare</li><li><strong>Logic break</strong>: early &quot;training ten years&quot; and late &quot;transform once&quot; intensity completely unequal</li><li><strong>Power inversion</strong>: new form when first appears crushes everything, a few chapters later becomes &quot;base form&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="iii-dragon-ball-s-energy-level-waste" tabindex="-1">III. Dragon Ball&#39;s Energy-Level Waste <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-dragon-ball-s-energy-level-waste" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Dragon Ball&#39;s Energy-Level Waste&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Combat waste</strong>: Dragon Ball&#39;s battles often destroy planets and cities, massive energy wasted in destruction</li><li><strong>Resurrection waste</strong>: Dragon Balls can casually resurrect the dead, life-death&#39;s karmic meaning dissolved</li><li><strong>Training waste</strong>: protagonist&#39;s training results often &quot;crushed on debut&quot; by new enemies, front-loaded effort wasted</li><li><strong>Supporting-character waste</strong>: Z Fighters except the protagonist group all reduced to backgrounds, no longer participating in battles</li></ul><h2 id="iv-dragon-ball-s-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" tabindex="-1">IV. Dragon Ball&#39;s Protagonist Uniqueness Dependency <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-dragon-ball-s-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Dragon Ball&#39;s Protagonist Uniqueness Dependency&quot;">​</a></h2><p>By the five-level standard, Dragon Ball&#39;s protagonist uniqueness dependency is <strong>extreme (Goku / solitary-tree type)</strong> — the entire cosmos&#39;s fate ultimately must be solved by Goku (or Vegeta) transforming. Other characters&#39; growth space is completely compressed by protagonist aura.</p><h2 id="v-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">V. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Assessment Dimension</th><th>Dragon Ball Score</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Realm self-consistency</td><td>Extremely low</td><td>Form naming arbitrary, realms and forms confused, no unified standard</td></tr><tr><td>Retcon risk</td><td>Extreme</td><td>Every stage overturns the previous stage&#39;s &quot;strongest&quot; setting</td></tr><tr><td>Ending risk</td><td>Medium</td><td>As long as sequels keep coming it never &quot;ends,&quot; but settings are already unmanageable</td></tr><tr><td>Plot kidnapping setting</td><td>Extremely severe</td><td>Power inflation&#39;s sole cause is &quot;needing stronger enemies&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Core problem</strong>: Dragon Ball from the start never established a law-level realm framework — what it has is only &quot;transformation forms.&quot; When forms are insufficient, new forms are invented. This is &quot;unanchored state&quot; — no law anchor, power inflation has no end and no direction.</p><h2 id="vi-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative-solution" tabindex="-1">VI. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative Solution <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative-solution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative Solution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How does Heng Yuan Zhou avoid unanchored inflation?</p><ul><li><strong>Law anchoring</strong>: realm definitions based on law dimensions, not transformation forms</li><li><strong>Dimensional leap</strong>: every realm corresponds to true existence-dimension advancement, not number getting bigger</li><li><strong>Myriad Races group</strong>: strong ones are a group, no pressure of &quot;only the protagonist carries&quot;</li><li><strong>Self-consistency verification</strong>: every realm&#39;s definition goes through law self-consistency verification, not changed due to plot needs</li></ul><h2 id="vii-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VII. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Dragon Ball&#39;s combat destruction and wasted training are enormous waste; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s every realm advancement has actual civilization contribution</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Dragon Ball&#39;s &quot;strong protect weak&quot; is essentially still &quot;strongest calls the shots&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s strong ones serve Myriad Races</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo locks the ceiling, Dragon Ball is infinite inflation — both are unanchored; Heng Yuan Zhou has law anchors</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Dragon Ball&#39;s protagonist group has only a few people; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s 20% Activation Strategy lets all Myriad Races have opportunity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s expansion is based on law self-consistency; Dragon Ball&#39;s inflation is based on transformation needs</li></ul><h2 id="viii-dragon-ball-model-s-lessons-for-cultivation-civilization" tabindex="-1">VIII. Dragon Ball Model&#39;s Lessons for Cultivation Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#viii-dragon-ball-model-s-lessons-for-cultivation-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VIII. Dragon Ball Model&#39;s Lessons for Cultivation Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Although Dragon Ball&#39;s power inflation model has many problems at the setting level, its lessons for cultivation civilization are not without value. Dragon Ball&#39;s &quot;train—break through—train again&quot; cycle rhythm, and the protagonist&#39;s spirit of constantly breaking through self through hard training, are themselves positive. The problem is not &quot;cultivation,&quot; but &quot;cultivation without a law framework&quot; — only training power not understanding laws, only transforming not knowing rules.</p><p>Heng Yuan Zhou absorbs Dragon Ball&#39;s spiritual core of &quot;hard training, never giving up,&quot; but puts it in a law-first framework: cultivation is not to transform to show enemies, but to understand cosmic laws, raise existence dimensions, serve Myriad Races symbiosis. Similarly &quot;protagonist keeps getting stronger,&quot; one is unanchored inflation, the other is anchored growth — this is the difference.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s power inflation is essentially the consequence of &quot;no law anchor&quot; — no law framework constrains realm definitions, the protagonist invents whatever strength is needed. Short-term, new forms and new transformations are indeed very hype; long-term, settings get messier and messier, readers already cannot remember how many forms there are. Heng Yuan Zhou starting from the law-first axiom gives every realm a clear law definition and existence dimension — not &quot;transform when stronger is needed,&quot; but &quot;entering new realm after understanding new law dimensions.&quot; This is the fundamental difference between &quot;anchored&quot; and &quot;unanchored.&quot;</p><p>In the final analysis, realm comparison · Dragon Ball power inflation&#39;s unanchored state described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./244-境界与未来-衡元宙境界体系的无限扩容性.html">244-Realm and Future Infinite Expandability</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane Transcendent Standards</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const m=n(r,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
